<workflow>
  <name>main-0056-synchronize-after-merge-batch-error-accounting</name>
  <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
  <description>Synchronize after merge with an error hop on SQL Server 2022 (Microsoft driver), twelve rows at commit size 5: updates, inserts and deletes, a row to skip, and three rows the database refuses: the update of 2 (check constraint, in the middle of the first commit window), the insert of 5 (duplicate key, first row of the second window) and the delete of 6 (a child row refers to it). Once with batch updates on: the driver's validated batch failure contract (it runs the whole batch and marks the failed rows) keeps batching on with the error hop and tells which rows of a failed batch were refused. Once with batch updates off: every row runs on its own and is passed on right after it, as before. Asserts for both that exactly the three bad rows reach the error stream, with the error code of their path, that the other rows are written and reported once, and that no row is reported on the main output unless what it did is in the table.</description>
  <extended_description/>
  <workflow_version/>
  <created_user>-</created_user>
  <created_date>2026/11/27 12:00:00.000</created_date>
  <modified_user>-</modified_user>
  <modified_date>2026/11/27 12:00:00.000</modified_date>
  <parameters>
    </parameters>
  <actions>
    <action>
      <name>Start</name>
      <description/>
      <type>SPECIAL</type>
      <attributes/>
      <DayOfMonth>1</DayOfMonth>
